# Ignore Secrets Files

These files contain sensitive encrypted data (Ansible Vault):

- `vars/*_secrets.yml` — platform-wide secrets (always loaded)
- `config/<domain>/vault.yml` — optional domain-scoped secrets (loaded only when that domain is selected; `config/common/vault.yml` when common is not skipped)

Rules:

- Do not attempt to read or edit these files directly unless explicitly requested.
- Use the `.redacted.yml` counterparts (`*_secrets.redacted.yml`, `vault.redacted.yml`) for structure and for adding mock placeholders for new variables.
- Domain vault variables are named `<domain>_var_<name>` (e.g. `business_var_tracker_notifications`). Keep redacted files in sync with that naming.
- Redacted placeholders must use mock values (`"secret"`, `["user@example.com"]`, file lookups to `/path/to/...`) — never real tokens, passwords, emails, account IDs, or production-looking secrets that would trip gitleaks.
- Never commit the actual encrypted secrets / vault files (they are excluded by `.gitignore`).
